Source: @officecli/officecli 1.0.162, the `skills/` payload installed by
`officecli skills install <name> codex` for:
word, excel, pptx, word-form, morph-ppt, pitch-deck, academic-paper,
data-dashboard, financial-model.

Changes from the upstream skills:
- Skill identifiers use the official CLI names (`word`, `excel`, `pptx`, …)
  instead of the `officecli-` file prefix.
- A Wanxiang delivery section was added to every skill: GB/T 9704-2012 for
  Chinese Word documents (title 方正小标宋简体 22 pt black, Heading 1 SimHei
  16 pt black, body FangSong_GB2312 16 pt), and enterprise template / brand
  rules for Excel and PowerPoint (微软雅黑, #2563EB, no default Calibri, no
  rainbow palettes).
- The upstream install instructions were replaced with the workspace-provided
  `officecli` / `officecli-create` tools.
- Cross-skill references were renamed to the new skill identifiers.

The binary itself is not vendored here; `@officecli/officecli` remains an
Apache-2.0 dependency installed from npm.